            {
              "id": "23fd80c3-9ed4-30a4-acb4-4e685d5a5209",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to the possibility that the source pointer may be null at the point where the memory copy operation is performed. The verdict for this call site is 'GENUINE', indicating high confidence in the issue. The code copies 8 bytes from a string literal to a destination buffer, but there are no explicit checks to ensure that the source pointer is not null. While the destination is likely safe (not a pointer-based member), the source could potentially be null, which would result in undefined behavior if the copy is attempted. No overlap between source and destination was detected, and the count argument is a literal value, but the lack of null checks on the source is a significant risk.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore performing the memory copy, ensure that the source pointer is not null. This can be done by adding an explicit check before the call:\n\n```cpp\nif (u8\"Infinity\" != nullptr) {\n    std::memcpy(result + sign, u8\"Infinity\", 8);\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, if the source is always a string literal (as in this case), it is guaranteed to be non-null by the C++ standard. However, if the analysis cannot guarantee this, and the source could be a variable, always check for null before copying. If the destination could also be null, add a similar check for the destination pointer.\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
