            {
              "id": "99b37686-cfff-36b6-81b7-2494d8e4a492",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to the possibility that the source pointer may be null when the memory copy operation is performed. The destination is a character pointer, and there is no evidence of a check to ensure that the source is not null before the operation. The count argument is a fixed literal (3), and there is no explicit null-terminator written after the copy. The analysis did not detect any overlap between source and destination, and the destination is likely a local or field array, reducing the risk of destination nullness. However, the lack of null checks for the source pointer is a significant concern, as dereferencing a null pointer leads to undefined behavior. This is why the finding is considered genuine and actionable.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore performing the memory copy operation, ensure that the source pointer is not null. This can be done by adding an explicit check before the call. For example:\n\n```cpp\nif (result != nullptr && u8\"NaN\" != nullptr) {\n    std::memcpy(result, u8\"NaN\", 3);\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, if the source is always a string literal (as in this case), you may not need to check for null, but if the analysis cannot guarantee this, it is safer to add the check. Always ensure that both source and destination pointers are valid before performing memory operations to avoid undefined behavior.\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
